## 16. Calculation Definitions

Document and implement the following metrics precisely.

**Returned-cheque count:** Number of distinct valid returned-cheque records under the documented record-identification rules.

**Returned-cheque value:** Sum of the amounts of the included returned-cheque records.

**Unique affected customers:** Count of distinct valid CX NUMBER values.

**Repeat-return customer:** Customer with at least the configured number of distinct returned-cheque records within the selected analysis period.

**Return frequency:** Number of returned-cheque records per customer, ADM, reason, or period.

**Average returned-cheque amount:** Total included returned-cheque value divided by the included returned-cheque count.

**Verified unrecovered exposure:** Sum of the remaining unrecovered amounts on cases with verified recovery status and valid recovery calculations. Exclude unresolved ambiguities from confirmed totals and report them separately.

**Recovered amount:** Total verified recovery amounts under the defined recovery accounting rules. Prevent duplicate counting when multiple recovery transactions exist.

**Recovery rate by value:** Verified recovered amount divided by the defined eligible returned-cheque value, expressed as a percentage. Document how partially recovered cases and the reporting period are handled.

**Period-over-period change:** Current-period metric minus previous comparable-period metric. Show percentage change only when the comparison denominator is meaningful and non-zero.

**Customer concentration:** Share of total included returned-cheque value contributed by a customer or selected customer group.

Use decimal-safe financial calculations and consistent currency formatting. Display Sri Lankan rupees (LKR) where the source data is denominated in LKR.

Do not treat missing values as zero without an explicit business rule.

